A||||8||camaro2fiero||1984 decklid side covers, whats the benefits?||||6||
Z||000000||camaro2fiero||05-05-2001||02:41 PM||||Hi everyone, A couple of questions.1. Do the 85 and up vented side panels,over the battery and  the other one on other side of decklid.can they be put on an 84? If they can,is there any benefit? Going to the Derby,well the local track to place a wager.SWo while I was waiting to go I thought of this insignificant question.My panels are flat and I was thinking maybe vented panel would bring so coolness to the engine.||||reg||6
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||05-05-2001||03:34 PM||||Yes, you hit the nail on the head!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>It will help in cooling<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||10
Z||000002||Tweek||05-05-2001||04:00 PM||||Ive got one of each on mine...   lol||||reg||1
Z||000003||Iron Duke Wellingsley||05-06-2001||01:05 PM||||I tried that on my '84, and the vented deck panels rattled a lot.  The flat panels are all one piece, where the vented ones are really two grills attached to each other with retaining clips.  <P>Now the flat panels are back on my car.  It looks a lot better.  I thought the center vents longitudinal pattern looked strange with the vented deck panel's horizontal vent pattern anyway.<P>You didn't ask, but black engine block paint works great on those babies.  They look years younger now.  Paint the center grill too.  It is easy and you will like the result.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||gtcash||05-06-2001||09:49 PM||||I did it to my 84 no problems, logically it has to be cooler in the engine compartment!<BR>I never had a temp check...<BR>I would like to mount ""pancake fans"" to them...suck the hot air out...good idea?||||reg||7
Z||000005||Songman||05-06-2001||11:19 PM||||I agree that the vents going in different directions doesn't look the best in the world, but it does help with cooling. And they won't rattle any more on an 84 than they do on any other year. And you can do things to help stop rattles if it does occur.<P>Bottom line as always is.. whatever you like... heheh<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||RacinRob||05-07-2001||10:54 AM||||To stop the rattle I just took the inner grill out... I've been told that this helps with cooling anyways. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||84Bill||05-07-2001||11:27 AM||||You will end up snapping off the little tabs on the vented covers.||||reg||4
Z||000008||qwikgta||05-07-2001||10:18 PM||||I bought a set of 84 covers off a fiero I found in a local junk yard.  I have removed the centers on my 88 coupe and when I am not driving the car I put the 84 covers on it.  Keeps out the rain and crud.  When I drive it I pop off the 84 covers and put back on the 88 "modified" ones.  I have a 79 mustang style scoop that I am going to put on the back and when I do that I may keep the 84 covers on it full time.  I am also thinking about painting them body color just to see how it looks.  I tell everyone who has modified the 85-88 covers to snag a set of 84's for when they are not driving it.   <P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
